ABOUT: Welcome to the commentary track!

glob:SCORE: The hours value of the current time. (See also [glob:PRESENT-TIME].)
	The Z-machine was originally designed to show `SCORE` and `MOVES` in the status line. In *Deadline*, these variables were repurposed to show a time in hours and minutes. A bit in the game file header tells the interpreter which way to format them.

glob:MOVES: The minutes value of the current time. (See also [glob:PRESENT-TIME].)
	The Z-machine was originally designed to show `SCORE` and `MOVES` in the status line. In *Deadline*, these variables were repurposed to show a time in hours and minutes. A bit in the game file header tells the interpreter which way to format them.

glob:PRESENT-TIME: The current time, stored as minutes after midnight (`H*60+M`). The game starts at 8:00 am.
	See also [glob:SCORE] and [glob:MOVES], which track the current time in a different way.
	
src:ACTIONS-109: The [glob:PRESENT-TIME] global is defined twice, which is not an error in ZIL.
	(The comment is wrong, though. Maybe it’s on Daylight Saving Time?)


rtn:V-ZORK: The `ZORK` command was removed from the grammar early on; no known release recognizes it. This vestige remains.

obj:STAIRS: This room lists itself as a scenery object (the `GLOBAL` property). This doesn’t seem to have any effect, but it doesn’t hurt the game either. It threw my Visible Zorker code for a loop though!

